course: dictionary
lesson: 5761
title: Words for travel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Luggage is the bags and suitcases you take with you when you travel. It is an uncountable noun, so we say «some luggage», not «a luggage» or «two luggages».
explain: Read the words around it. «People with prams, wheelchairs and luggage go first in a station lift, because they cannot use stairs or escalators.» Prams and wheelchairs are big things that are hard to carry up stairs, so luggage must be bags and cases that are hard to carry too. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Travel words often add a word in front of luggage. «Hand luggage» is the bag you keep with you on a plane. Luggage in the hold is the bag that goes underneath, away from you. Words such as «coach» and «power bank» appear near luggage in travel too, so the topic helps you guess.
fact: Luggage means the bags and suitcases you take when you travel.
fact: «Luggage» is uncountable: you say some luggage, not a luggage.
fact: «Hand luggage» is the bag you keep with you on a plane, not the one that goes in the hold.
fact: A «coach» is a big bus with luggage space underneath.
fact: A «power bank» goes in hand luggage on a plane, not in a checked bag, so someone can reach it if it gets hot.
exercise: «People with prams, wheelchairs and luggage go first in a station lift.» What is luggage? | A kind of station lift | A type of wheelchair | The stairs and escalators in a station | *Bags and suitcases you take when you travel
exercise: «On planes a power bank goes in hand luggage, not in a checked bag.» Where should a power bank go on a plane? | In a checked bag in the hold | On the seat next to you with no cover | *In your hand luggage | Under the plane's wing
exercise: Find and copy the word for a big bus with luggage space underneath. «A coach is a big bus with luggage space underneath.» | battery | *coach | lift | prams
test: Which is correct? | a luggage | a luggages | *some luggage | two luggages
test: «People with prams, wheelchairs and luggage go first in a station lift.» What most likely means prams here? | Pieces of luggage | *Baby buggies | Train tickets | Station cafés
exam: Jayden says hand luggage and luggage mean exactly the same thing. What is the best answer? | No, luggage is only what goes in the hold | Yes, but only on trains and coaches | No, hand luggage is one kind of luggage, the bag you keep with you | *Yes, they are the same, so you can use either for any bag
